.TH "Docv::Cell" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Cell \- One grid cell: a grapheme with its rendition.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBstruct Docv::Cell\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
One grid cell: a grapheme with its rendition. A wide grapheme occupies a
cell of width 2 followed by a continuation cell of width 0. The struct has
no padding (12 bytes), so rows compare with \fB\%memcmp\fR.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBBLANK = Cell.new(\(aq \(aq)\fR
A blank cell in the default style.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.blank(style : UInt16) : Cell\fR
A blank cell in \fIstyle\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.continuation(style : UInt16) : Cell\fR
The continuation cell after a wide cell in \fIstyle\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.from(cluster : String, style : UInt16) : Cell\fR
Builds the cell of a grapheme cluster.
.PP
\fBdef self.new(ch : Char, style : UInt16 = 0_u16, width : UInt8 = 1_u8, cluster : Int32 = 0)\fR
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.PP
\fBdef ch : Char\fR
.PP
\fBdef cluster : Int32\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef continuation? : Bool\fR
True for the second half of a wide grapheme.
.PP
\fBdef style : UInt16\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef text(io : IO) : Nil\fR
Writes the grapheme of this cell.
.PP
\fBdef width : UInt8\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef with_style(style : UInt16) : Cell\fR
Returns this cell with another rendition.
